What graphql-js 17 (prettier 3.9.9's graphql parser) reads and the 2021 upstream grammar does not, each commented
where it changes: keywords as names (`word`), several directives on a field, descriptions on operations, fragments
and variables, legacy fragment variables and fragment arguments, escapes in strings, `extend schema` with
directives alone, directives on a directive definition and `extend directive`. A comma is whitespace (an extra)
everywhere, so no rule lists one.

